      "derivedAnswer": "B: 15°",
      "mathematicalReason": "Write x = ∠BAO and draw OB. Since AB = OD = OB, triangle AOB is isosceles, giving ∠AOB = x and ∠ABO = 180° − 2x. Because A, B, E are collinear in that order, ∠OBE = 2x. The equal radii OB = OE then give ∠BEO = 2x, which also equals ∠AEO. Meanwhile, ∠AOE = 180° − 45° = 135°. The angle sum in triangle AOE yields x + 2x + 135° = 180°, hence x = 15°. This directly supports the proposed isosceles-triangle assessment and supporting scopes.",
